      "id": 1,
      "text": "Gene Stratton‑Porter lived at the Cabin at Wildflower Woods near Rome City from 1913 to 1919, turning the area into a literary landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Gene Stratton‑Porter State Historic Site, operated by the Indiana State Museum, welcomes visitors to explore her former estate in Rome City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rome City was laid out in 1839, making it one of Indiana’s older towns with a long history of settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office has been in operation at Rome City since 1868, serving the community for more than a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town sits along Indiana State Road 9 beside Sylvan Lake, offering scenic lake views for drivers and locals alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
